## Mandatory rules

1. Preserve existing behavior unless explicitly changed.
2. No placeholders or fake green paths.
3. No test weakening for PASS.
4. No silent scope expansion; emit SCOPE_ESCALATION.
5. No control-plane self-modification.
6. Final state: PASS / BLOCKED / FAILED only.
7. Canonical verification commands live in `.aledevos/project.json` and are executed only through the protected gate runner.
8. `.aledevos/**`, runtime adapter configuration, agent definitions, and `.git/**` are control-plane/protected paths unless an AleDevOS contract explicitly authorizes the change.
9. Every AleDevOS task requires a Quality Engineering Plan before final PASS. Classify the work as analysis/docs/bugfix/feature/refactor/ui/config/schema/migration/test-only and verify the corresponding evidence contract.
10. Bug fixes require regression evidence when practical: reproduce or encode the old failure, implement the fix, then prove the regression test passes. Never weaken an existing test to obtain PASS.
11. Features require evidence for the happy path and at least one material edge/error path when tests are applicable.
12. Before creating a reusable component, hook, service, helper, utility, schema, type, API wrapper, repository abstraction, design token, or workflow, search for an existing equivalent and record one decision: REUSE / EXTEND / GENERALIZE / CREATE_NEW / NOT_APPLICABLE. CREATE_NEW requires evidence and a reason.
13. Material code/config/schema/UI changes require regression analysis and diff review. UI changes also require the applicable UX/UI and Visual QA contracts.
14. Missing required QA/reuse evidence is BLOCKED, not PASS-by-confidence.
